MS header. The h_ crop (y0–260) I described as \\\"基线与人群总览\\\"... Actually wait, the h_ crops: h_efficacy-safety-matrix-768.png and h_baseline-overview-768.png — I read them and the first showed 基线， second 矩阵. But top_efficacy-safety-matrix-768.png (y0–1200 same file) shows 矩阵 heading. Contradiction — unless I misread the h_ images. The h_ read responses: image1 I saw as \\\"基线与人群总览\\\"?? The read tool just returned images; my interpretation may have been swapped due to ordering. Given direct evidence now: matrix file top crop clearly shows \\\"疗效与安全性矩阵\\\" heading. And baseline file (mtx768_a/b crops) shows 基线特征. And disposition file shows 试验完成情况. So NO swap — my earlier swap conclusion was a misreading artifact. Good: retract that defect.\\n\\nAlso the \\\"未列示\\\" truncation: in mtx768_b crop, rightmost column shows \\\"未列/\\\" cut — appears on baseline page too. And disposition shows \\\"未列\\\" cut. Confirmed real truncation across pages at 768 (safety, overview, baseline, disposition data tables). But efficacy page at 768 was fine (8 cols fit). Actually baseline table has 8 cols too but truncated. Efficacy table fit within card with padding; baseline table's last column 分子 shows \\\"未列\\\" partially clipped at x≈760. Hmm wait in mtx768_a the table shows 分子 column values \\\"未列.\\\" cut. So defect stands: at 768, several data tables clip the last column's text (\\\"未列示\\\" → \\\"未列\\\"). BUT maybe the character is fully \\\"未列示\\\" and rendering shows \\\"未列\\\" + partial \\\"示\\\"? In zoom /tmp/safety768_right.png at 3x, we saw \\\"未列/\\\" with partial glyph — clipped mid-character. Confirmed real.\\n\\nHowever: is there horizontal scrolling available within the table container? If the table has internal horizontal scroll, then content is accessible but requires dragging — which the brief says is a fail criterion for the safety matrix specifically (matrix = heatmap; the heatmaps fit). The data tables are a separate concern but still readability defect.\\n\\nActu