on of 46 children!). So sequence: page keydown handler hid results + preventDefault? No — if preventDefault ran, native clear wouldn't happen. If preventDefault DIDN'T run (handler not firing), native clear → input event → showResults reopens with full list. Observed: hidden=false, q=''. So handler did NOT run.\\n\\nBut synthetic dispatch ran the handler. Difference between synthetic and real? Real keydown: my probe saw defaultPrevented false. Portal's listener was registered earlier (script executed before my evaluate) → runs first. Unless portal.js listener attached to a DIFFERENT element: check line ~11-20: `searchInput = document.getElementById(\\\"global-search-input\\\")`? Verify.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_DPq1itfrIVljL6ucUqIoBuiR\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"sed -n 1,30p \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/portal.js\\\"\",\"i\":\"Reading portal.js header\"},\"intent\":\"Reading portal.js header\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":920,\"output\":636,\"cacheRead\":69888,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":71444,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079611338,\"responseId\":\"msg_tX7VWQrN225hqW44rWcGDCBj\",\"duration\":18561.46533300006,\"ttft\":3565.997083000024},\"toolResults\":[{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_DPq1itfrIVljL6ucUqIoBuiR\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/**\\n * Portal JS — global search, grouped nav, mobile toggle, keyboard support.\\n *\\n * Zero remote dependencies; works from file://.\\n * Consumes window.__SEARCH_INDEX__ (inline and/or search-index.js).\\n */\\n(function () {\\n  \\\"use strict\\\";\\n\\n  var searchInput = document.getElementById(\\\"global-search-input\\\")