-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/evidence-drawer.js\\\"\",\"i\":\"Checking Escape listeners both files\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"message_end\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Attachment is direct on #global-search-input. Real Escape didn't trigger it? But my probe on same element saw the event with defaultPrevented=false... portal handler registered first runs first — if it ran, defaultPrevented would be true by the time my listener runs. Unless portal.js threw an error during initial execution before attaching listeners — but typing '疗效' DID show filtered results (10 items), which requires the input listener. So input listener works for 'input' events. The keydown listener is attached in same block. So it should fire.\\n\\nHmm wait — maybe there are two `input` elements? No, count=1.\\n\\nCritical check: maybe the real keydown handler ran, set hidden=true, preventDefault… then something reopened: the 'input' event from native clear would set hidden=false again AND q=''. But preventDefault should have stopped native clear. UNLESS the browser clears the search input NOT as default action of keydown but on keypress/other — for input[type=search], Chromium clears on Escape keydown default action (cancelable). preventDefault in keydown stops it. Since query was cleared, preventDefault didn't happen.\\n\\nOR: focus wasn't in the input when I pressed Escape! After typing... tab.press sends to focused element — inp.click() focused it, typing worked. Focus retained. My probe listener on input saw the event → keydown reached input. So portal's keydown listener (registered earlier on same element, bubble phase) ran before my probe... defaultPrevented false at my probe → portal listener didn't preventDefault. So portal listener didn't run or returned early: `if (!searchResults || searchResults.hidden)` → if hidden was TRUE at that moment, returns early (only handles Enter). Was hidden true? After typing, results visible... unless typing '疗效' — the results showed. s1 earlier confirmed hidden=false. But in THIS run I didn't check hidden before Escape. If some earlier action left hidden=true while panel visually... no, panel was visible.\\n\\nWait, actually: maybe showResults sets `searchResults.hidden = false` but ALSO the CSS display:block overrides hidden anyway. Not relevant to handler logic.\\n\\nHmm, one more possibility: TWO handlers on window for Escape from evidence-drawer.js (line 1081) with capture that calls closeResponsiveNavigation and stopImmediatePropagation? Check lines around 1075-1090.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_hMkVQ3KBy107M6tUALgUy7Vb\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"sed -n 1070,1100p \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/portal.js\\\"; grep -n \\\"1081\\\" \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/evidence-drawer.js\\\" >/dev/null; sed -n 1075,1095p \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/evidence-drawer.js\\\"\",\"i\":\"Checking Escape listeners both files\"},\"intent\":\"Checking Escape listeners both files\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":1080,\"output\":734,\"cacheRead\":70656,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":72470,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079629910,\"responseId\":\"msg_7JicUGqhKOAD3m0giYBTlHCK\",\"duration\":21059.53420799994,\"ttft\":3204.638082999969,\"completedAt\":1788079650992}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_execution_start\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_hMkVQ3KBy107M6tUALgUy7