 wrap the actual portal handler by checking via getEventListeners? Not available. Instead, test with focus NOT via click but via keyboard Tab? Or test on webkit? Time. Alternative: run real Escape on the safety page where I type then IMMEDIATELY press Escape without clicking menu etc. Or test with page.keyboard.down('Escape')? Same.\\n\\nHonestly: could puppeteer 'Escape' trigger two keydowns? Log showed exactly one. defaultPrevented false at my listener — but wait, my listener is on input, registered AFTER portal's. Both bubble phase on same node: registration order — portal's first. If portal's ran preventDefault, my listener sees defaultPrevented=true. Observed false → portal's keydown handler did not run for this event. But synthetic event on same node DID run portal's handler (hidden became true). Difference: trusted vs untrusted... The handler has no isTrusted check.\\n\\nOH WAIT. Maybe there are TWO elements with id 'global-search-input'? getElementById returns first in document order. Page may contain a second header (e.g., a print header or a duplicate in menu). count of '.site-header__search input' = 1, but maybe another input with same id outside .site-header__search. Check.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_start\",\"contentIndex\":1}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"{\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"\\\"content\\\": \\\"\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"{\\\\\\\"\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"action\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"\\\\\\\":\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"as