hed to a DIFFERENT `searchInput` element reference because the DOM was re-rendered after portal.js loaded (portal.js ran, grabbed element; later JS replaced header HTML)? If the node was replaced, portal's handlers would be on a detached node; typing works because... typing is native; but results rendering requires the 'input' listener which works → same node. OK.\\n\\nWait, actually did results really filter via JS? The results panel showed 10 filtered items — yes JS-driven.\\n\\nHmm, let me test directly: dispatch isTrusted vs not — real press creates trusted event. Could portal.js keydown listener be attached with `{capture:...}`? No. Could `searchResults.hidden` at press time be true while panel visible due to CSS override? If hidden=true (attribute) but CSS display:block makes it visible — then my earlier s1 check `hidden:false` — I did check: s1.hidden=false. So no.\\n\\nLet me instrument: wrap the actual portal handler by checking via getEventListeners? Not available. Instead, test with focus NOT via click but via keyboard Tab? Or test on webkit? Time. Alternative: run real Escape on the safety page where I type then IMMEDIATELY press Escape without clicking menu etc. Or test with page.keyboard.down('Escape')? Same.\\n\\nHonestly: could puppeteer 'Escape' trigger two keydowns? Log showed exactly one. defaultPrevented false at my listener — but wait, my listener is on input, registered AFTER portal's. Both bubble phase on same node: registration order — portal's first. If portal's ran preventDefault, my listener sees defaultPrevented=true. Observed false → portal's keydown handler did not run for this event. But synthetic event on same node DID run portal's handler (hidden became true). Difference: trusted vs untrusted... The handler has no isTrusted check.\\n\\nOH WAIT. Maybe there are TWO elements with id 'global-search-input'? getElementById returns first in document order. Page may contain a second header (e.g., a print header or a duplicate in menu). count of '.site-header__search input' = 1, but maybe another input with same id outside .site-header__search. Check.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_Cel1yIJRMyYajTyesI4kCAHT\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"content\":\"{\\\"action\\\": \\\"run\\\", \\\"code\\\": \\\"return await tab.evaluate(() => { const all=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-input')]; const r=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-results')]; return {inputs: all.length, results: r.length, portals: [...document.querySelectorAll('script')].map(s=>s.src.split('/').pop()).filter(Boolean)}; })\\\"}\",\"i\":\"Checking duplicate ids and scripts\",\"path\":\"xd://browser\"},\"intent\":\"Checking duplicate ids and scripts\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":1085,\"output\":751,\"cacheRead\":71680,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":73516,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079651009,\"responseId\":\"msg_diUTtYGzyB9UO6Skh4KEYrMc\",\"duration\":18706.02570800006,\"ttft\":3635.2097080000676},\"toolResults\":[{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_Cel1yIJRMyYajTyesI4kCAHT\",\"toolName\":\"write\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"inputs\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"results\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"portals\\\": [\\n    \\\"search-index.js\\\",\\n    \\\"portal.js\\\",\\n    \\\"echarts.min.js\\\",\\n    \\\"evidence-drawer.js\\\",\\n    \\\"report-b.js\\\",\\n    \\\"charts.js\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\"}],\"details\":{\"xdev\":{\"tool\":\"browser\",\"mode\":\"execute\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"run\",\"code\":\"return await tab.evaluate(() => { const all=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-input')]; const r=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-results')]; return {inputs: all.length, results: r.length, portals: [...document.querySelectorAll('script')].map(s=>s.src.split('/').pop()).filter(Boolea