\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"thinking_end\",\"contentIndex\":0,\"content\":\"Decisive: portal handler DID run (attr hidden→true), THEN hidden→false and input cleared. So order: keydown handler hid results + preventDefault... but query still cleared and results reopened. That means preventDefault did NOT block native clearing in this Chromium (or the clear isn't the default action of this keydown), and the 'input' event from clearing reopened results via showResults(''). Net user-visible behavior in this Chromium: Escape clears the query and leaves the full default result list visible; second Escape hides panel. The code comment explicitly says preventDefault \\\"stops Chromium input[type=search] from clearing the query\\\" — but empirically in this Chromium (headless, via puppeteer CDP) it did NOT. Whether real-user Chromium behaves the same is uncertain; playwright evidence claims pass. Hmm — but the mutation trace is from MY browser session, real trusted key. So claim \\\"Escape关闭结果并保留查询\\\" is not robust: it depends on preventDefault blocking native clear, which failed here.\\n\\nActually wait — is it possible keydown handler ran but preventDefault works only if event is cancelable keydown... CDP rawKeyDown events: for input[type=search], the clearing in Chromium happens in `SearchFieldCancelButtonElement`?/ Actually Escape clearing happens in `TextFieldInputType::handleKeydownEvent`? In WebKit/Blink, Escape clearing of search field is in `SearchInputType::handleKeydownEvent` — handled BEFORE default event processing? Blink: HTMLInputElement::defaultEventHandler → textfield handles Escape. If JS preventDefault sets defaultPrevented, defaultEventHandler is skipped. Puppeteer sends RawKeyDown for Escape; maybe the renderer treats it and preventDefault from JS still applies... Empirically it did NOT apply. My session: Chrome headless (which version?). Whatever — real trusted key, observed behavior stands for this environment.\\n\\nGiven playwright evidence claims pass and my puppeteer test fails, this is a cross-harness discrepancy. As a reviewer I flag: behavior fragile — relies on preventDefault suppressing native search-clear; observed failure in headless Chromium via CDP; net effect for users could be query cleared + panel stays open showing default list. Recommend: in Escape handler ALSO set a flag to ignore the subsequent input event, or don't reopen results on empty query unless focused... Remediation concrete.\\n\\nMenu focus defect: confirmed in code (no focus call) — solid.\\n\\n768 table clipping: confirmed solid (overflow-x auto, no hint, text visually cut at edge in screenshots).\\n\\nI've spent enough. Check quickly: does the 1024 screenshot truncation exist? At 1024 stacked layout fine. At 1440 fine (overview-1440 tables looked complete).\\n\\nAlso confirm \\\"APPOIN T–PNH\\\" wrap — seen in screenshots; minor typography.\\n\\nCharts: bar charts fine; bubble chart single point with explanation note; OK. Colors: orange/blue consistent, colorblind-safe-ish; severity heatmap color scale visible. Text: Chinese natural; \\\"未列示/未公开/不适用\\\" distinguished; \\\"已报告值\\\" status present.\\n\\nNow stop server & close browser, write report.\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_start\",\"contentIndex\":1}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"{\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"\\\"content\\\": \\\"\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"{\\\\\\\"\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"action\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message_update\",\"assistantMessageEvent\":{\"type\":\"toolcall_delta\",\"contentIndex\":1,\"delta\":\"\\\\\\\":\"}}\n{\"ty