ntent is accessible but requires dragging — which the brief says is a fail criterion for the safety matrix specifically (matrix = heatmap; the heatmaps fit). The data tables are a separate concern but still readability defect.\\n\\nActually wait — check whether tables at 768 have overflow-x scroll: the table might be wider than viewport with scroll. The screenshot shows rightmost column cut exactly at viewport edge, suggesting overflow. Check live: compute in browser. Let's do live browser reproduction now: serve report html, check table scrollWidth vs clientWidth, test menu search, keyboard Enter/Space on evidence cell, Escape close.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Retracting the filename-swap suspicion — direct crops confirm each file's content matches its name. Now a live browser pass to verify table clipping/scroll and interactions.\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_DM2AJrCTgVJ6fyDPNTRRlEmr\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"ls \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/artifacts/report-b-pnh/\\\" 2>/dev/null; ls \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html\\\" 2>/dev/null | head\",\"i\":\"Locating report html\"},\"intent\":\"Locating report html\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":7623,\"output\":1119,\"cacheRead\":39936,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":48678,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079084271,\"responseId\":\"msg_RuA7224OCf0fEh4UefAIty19\",\"duration\":33678.11087500001,\"ttft\":3188.4160409999895},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_DM2AJrCTgVJ6fyDPNTRRlEmr\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"adherence.html\\nassets\\nbaseline-demographics.html\\nbaseline