 So sequence: page keydown handler hid results + preventDefault? No — if preventDefault ran, native clear wouldn't happen. If preventDefault DIDN'T run (handler not firing), native clear → input event → showResults reopens with full list. Observed: hidden=false, q=''. So handler did NOT run.\\n\\nBut synthetic dispatch ran the handler. Difference between synthetic and real? Real keydown: my probe saw defaultPrevented false. Portal's listener was registered earlier (script executed before my evaluate) → runs first. Unless portal.js listener attached to a DIFFERENT element: check line ~11-20: `searchInput = document.getElementById(\\\"global-search-input\\\")`? Verify.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_DPq1itfrIVljL6ucUqIoBuiR\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"sed -n 1,30p \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/portal.js\\\"\",\"i\":\"Reading portal.js header\"},\"intent\":\"Reading portal.js header\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":920,\"output\":636,\"cacheRead\":69888,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":71444,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079611338,\"responseId\":\"msg_tX7VWQrN225hqW44rWcGDCBj\",\"duration\":18561.46533300006,\"ttft\":3565.997083000024},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_DPq1itfrIVljL6ucUqIoBuiR\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"/**\\n * Portal JS — global search, grouped nav, mobile toggle, keyboard support.\\n *\\n * Zero remote dependencies; works from file://.\\n * Consumes window.__SEARCH_INDEX__ (inline and/or search-index.js).\\n */\\n(function () {\\n  \\\"use strict\\\";\\n\\n  var searchInput = document.getElementById(\\\"global-search-input\\\");\\n  var searchResults = document.getElementById(\\\"global-search-results\\\");\\n  var searchIndex = window.__SEARCH_INDEX__ || [];\\n  var focusedIdx = -1;\\n\\n  function getQuery() {\\n    return ((searchInput && searchInput.value) || \\\"\\\").trim().toLowerCase();\\n  }\\n\\n  function scoreEntry(query, entry) {\\n    var score = 0;\\n    var titleLower = String(entry.title || \\\"\\\").toLowerCase();\\n    if (titleLower.indexOf(query) !== -1) {\\n      score += 100;\\n    }\\n    var keywords = entry.keywords || [];\\n    for (var i = 0; i < keywords.length; i += 1) {\\n      var kw = String(keywords[i] || \\\"\\\").toLowerCase();\\n      if (kw.indexOf(query) !== -1 || query.indexOf(kw) !== -1) {\\n        score += 10;\\n      }\\n\\n\\nWall time: 0.00 seconds\"}],\"details\":{\"timeoutSeconds\":300,\"wallTimeMs\":1.6591669999761507},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1788079629905},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Attachment is direct on #global-search-input. Real Escape didn't trigger it? But my probe on same element saw the event with defaultPrevented=false... portal handler registered first runs first — if it ran, defaultPrevented would be true by the time my listener runs. Unless portal.js threw an error during initial execution before attaching listeners — but typing '疗效' DID show filtered results (10 items), which requires the input listener. So input listener works for 'input' events. The keydown listener is attached in same block. So it should fire.\\n\\nHmm wait — maybe there are two `input` elements? No, count=1.\\n\\nCritical check: maybe the real keydown handler ran, set hidden=true, preventDefault… then something reopened: the 'input' event from native clear would set hidden=false again AND q=''. But preventDefault should have stopped native clear. UNLESS the browser clears the search input NOT as default action of keydown but on keypress/other — for input[type=search], Chromium clears on Escape keydown default action (cancelable). preventDefault in keydown stops it. Since query was cleared, preventDefault didn't happen.\\n\\nOR: focus wasn't in the input when I pressed Escape! After typing... tab.press sends to focused element — inp.click() focused it, typing worked. Focus retained. My probe listener on input saw the event → keydown reached input. So portal's keydown listener (registered earlier on same element, bubble phase) ran before my probe... defaultPrevented false at my probe → portal listener didn't preventDefault. So portal listener didn't run or returned early: `if (!searchResults || searchResults.hidden)` → if hidden was TRUE at that moment, returns early (only handles Enter). Was hidden true? After typing, results visible... unless typing '疗效' — the results showed. s1 earlier confirmed hidden=false. But in THIS run I didn't check hidden before Escape. If some earlier action left hidden=true while panel visually... no, panel was visible.\\n\\nWait, actually: maybe showResults sets `searchResults.hidden = false` but ALSO the CSS display:block overrides hidden anyway. Not relevant to handler logic.\\n\\nHmm, one more possibility: TWO handlers on window for Escape from evidence-drawer.js (line 1081) with capture that calls closeResponsiveNavigation and stopImmediatePropagation? Check lines around 1075-1090.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_hMkVQ3KBy107M6tUALgUy7Vb\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"sed -n 1070,1100p \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/portal.js\\\"; grep -n \\\"1081\\\" \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/evidence-drawer.js\\\" >/dev/null; sed -n 1075,1095p \\\"output/acceptance/task-6.10/phase-6-acceptance-package-20260830/b-pnh-interaction-repair-20260830/reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html/assets/evidence-drawer.js\\\"\",\"i\":\"Checking Escape listeners both files\"},\"intent\":\"Checking Escape listeners both files\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":1080,\"output\":734,\"cacheRead\":70656,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":72470,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079629910,\"responseId\":\"msg_7JicUGqhKOAD3m0giYBTlHCK\",\"duration\":21059.53420799994,\"ttft\":3204.638082999969},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_hMkVQ3KBy107M6tUALgUy7Vb\",\"toolName\":\"bash\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"      }\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  if (filterClose) {\\n    filterClose.addEventListener(\\\"click\\\", function () {\\n      closePanel();\\n    });\\n  }\\n\\n  document.addEventListener(\\\"keydown\\\", function (e) {\\n    if (e.key !== \\\"Escape\\\" && e.key !== \\\"Esc\\\") return;\\n    if (window.__EVIDENCE_DRAWER__ && window.__EVIDENCE_DRAWER__.isOpen()) return;\\n    if (filterPanel && filterPanel.hasAttribute(\\\"open\\\")) {\\n      closePanel();\\n    }\\n  });\\n\\n  for (var fi = 0; fi < filterItems.length; fi++) {\\n    (function (item) {\\n      item.addEventListener(\\\"click\\\", function () {\\n        if (item.getAttribute(\\\"aria-disabled\\\") === \\\"true\\\" || item.disabled) {\\n          return;\\n        }\\n        var dim = item.getAttribute(\\\"data-dim\\\");\\n        var val = item.getAttribute(\\\"data-val\\\");\\n        var scope = item.getAttribute(\\\"data-scope\\\") || \\\"page\\\";\\n        var mid = item.getAttribute(\\\"data-module-id\\\") || \\\"\\\";\\n        if (!dim || !val) return;\\n        var bucket = getActiveBucket(scope, mid);\\n        if (!bucket[dim]) bucket[dim] = [];\\n\\n\\nWall time: 0.01 seconds\"}],\"details\":{\"timeoutSeconds\":300,\"wallTimeMs\":5.156000000075437},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1788079651002},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Nothing stops propagation. So why didn't the input keydown handler preventDefault on real Escape?\\n\\nNew hypothesis: Puppeteer's Escape press in headless Chromium: the browser performs the search-input clear via a \\\"before keydown\\\" native path? In Chrome, Escape clearing of search field happens in NativeWebKeyboardEvent handling before dispatch? Actually the clear happens as default action. preventDefault on keydown from JS does prevent it (that's the documented behavior and the code comment references it — so it worked in playwright testing).\\n\\nMaybe the difference: my probe showed event reaches input listener — but is it possible portal.js's listener is attached to a DIFFERENT `searchInput` element reference because the DOM was re-rendered after portal.js loaded (portal.js ran, grabbed element; later JS replaced header HTML)? If the node was replaced, portal's handlers would be on a detached node; typing works because... typing is native; but results rendering requires the 'input' listener which works → same node. OK.\\n\\nWait, actually did results really filter via JS? The results panel showed 10 filtered items — yes JS-driven.\\n\\nHmm, let me test directly: dispatch isTrusted vs not — real press creates trusted event. Could portal.js keydown listener be attached with `{capture:...}`? No. Could `searchResults.hidden` at press time be true while panel visible due to CSS override? If hidden=true (attribute) but CSS display:block makes it visible — then my earlier s1 check `hidden:false` — I did check: s1.hidden=false. So no.\\n\\nLet me instrument: wrap the actual portal handler by checking via getEventListeners? Not available. Instead, test with focus NOT via click but via keyboard Tab? Or test on webkit? Time. Alternative: run real Escape on the safety page where I type then IMMEDIATELY press Escape without clicking menu etc. Or test with page.keyboard.down('Escape')? Same.\\n\\nHonestly: could puppeteer 'Escape' trigger two keydowns? Log showed exactly one. defaultPrevented false at my listener — but wait, my listener is on input, registered AFTER portal's. Both bubble phase on same node: registration order — portal's first. If portal's ran preventDefault, my listener sees defaultPrevented=true. Observed false → portal's keydown handler did not run for this event. But synthetic event on same node DID run portal's handler (hidden became true). Difference: trusted vs untrusted... The handler has no isTrusted check.\\n\\nOH WAIT. Maybe there are TWO elements with id 'global-search-input'? getElementById returns first in document order. Page may contain a second header (e.g., a print header or a duplicate in menu). count of '.site-header__search input' = 1, but maybe another input with same id outside .site-header__search. Check.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_Cel1yIJRMyYajTyesI4kCAHT\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"content\":\"{\\\"action\\\": \\\"run\\\", \\\"code\\\": \\\"return await tab.evaluate(() => { const all=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-input')]; const r=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-results')]; return {inputs: all.length, results: r.length, portals: [...document.querySelectorAll('script')].map(s=>s.src.split('/').pop()).filter(Boolean)}; })\\\"}\",\"i\":\"Checking duplicate ids and scripts\",\"path\":\"xd://browser\"},\"intent\":\"Checking duplicate ids and scripts\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":1085,\"output\":751,\"cacheRead\":71680,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":73516,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079651009,\"responseId\":\"msg_diUTtYGzyB9UO6Skh4KEYrMc\",\"duration\":18706.02570800006,\"ttft\":3635.2097080000676},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_Cel1yIJRMyYajTyesI4kCAHT\",\"toolName\":\"write\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"inputs\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"results\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"portals\\\": [\\n    \\\"search-index.js\\\",\\n    \\\"portal.js\\\",\\n    \\\"echarts.min.js\\\",\\n    \\\"evidence-drawer.js\\\",\\n    \\\"report-b.js\\\",\\n    \\\"charts.js\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\"}],\"details\":{\"xdev\":{\"tool\":\"browser\",\"mode\":\"execute\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"run\",\"code\":\"return await tab.evaluate(() => { const all=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-input')]; const r=[...document.querySelectorAll('#global-search-results')]; return {inputs: all.length, results: r.length, portals: [...document.querySelectorAll('script')].map(s=>s.src.split('/').pop()).filter(Boolean)}; })\"},\"tier\":\"exec\",\"inner\":{\"action\":\"run\",\"name\":\"main\",\"browser\":\"headless\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:8931/overview.html\",\"result\":\"{\\n  \\\"inputs\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"results\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"portals\\\": [\\n    \\\"search-index.js\\\",\\n    \\\"portal.js\\\",\\n    \\\"echarts.min.js\\\",\\n    \\\"evidence-drawer.js\\\",\\n    \\\"report-b.js\\\",\\n    \\\"charts.js\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\"}}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1788079669741},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"One input, one results. So portal's keydown handler should run on real Escape... but empirically didn't preventDefault. One more possibility: `tab.press('Escape')` from this browser tool might synthesize events differently (e.g., only keyup or rawKeyDown where defaultPrevented can't stop native clear?). Chromium performs search-field clearing on rawKeyDown? In Chromium, Escape-to-clear for search inputs is handled in the renderer as part of keydown default handling; puppeteer sends RawKeyDown + Char + KeyUp. For keys like Escape, puppeteer sends 'rawKeyDown'. JS keydown listeners DO fire for rawKeyDown. preventDefault should still work...\\n\\nTime to stop deep-diving. Evidence position: code intends Escape→hide+preserve; synthetic dispatch confirms handler logic works; playwright evidence says pass; my puppeteer real-key run shows native clear winning (hidden stayed false because input event reopened results with default list). This smells like a genuine race in real Chromium: input event fires after keydown (clear happens as default even when... no). Actually here's a coherent explanation: preventDefault DID run and hidden=true was set. But then... q became ''? No.\\n\\nLet me do one decisive test: after real Escape, check hidden attribute IMMEDIATELY (synchronously) — I'll add a MutationObserver on hidden attr and input listener logging order.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_hHBiF0QfKYmrPzTwWW3nMfoP\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"content\":\"{\\\"action\\\": \\\"run\\\", \\\"code\\\": \\\"await tab.evaluate(() => { window.__ev=[]; const r=document.getElementById('global-search-results'); const i=document.getElementById('global-search-input'); new MutationObserver(m=>m.forEach(x=>window.__ev.push(['attr', x.attributeName, r.hidden]))).observe(r,{attributes:true, attributeFilter:['hidden']}); i.addEventListener('input', ()=>window.__ev.push(['input', i.value, r.hidden])); i.value='疗效'; i.dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true})); i.focus(); }); await tab.press('Escape'); await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,300)); return await tab.evaluate(() => ({ev: window.__ev, hidden: document.getElementById('global-search-results').hidden, q: document.getElementById('global-search-input').value}));\\\"}\",\"i\":\"Tracing Escape mutation sequence\",\"path\":\"xd://browser\"},\"intent\":\"Tracing Escape mutation sequence\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":902,\"output\":551,\"cacheRead\":72704,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":74157,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079669746,\"responseId\":\"msg_nBA82DDjptAbHVZdZ7Xc99sp\",\"duration\":13311.708250000025,\"ttft\":3074.7872080000816},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_hHBiF0QfKYmrPzTwWW3nMfoP\",\"toolName\":\"write\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"ev\\\": [\\n    [\\n      \\\"input\\\",\\n      \\\"疗效\\\",\\n      false\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"attr\\\",\\n      \\\"hidden\\\",\\n      true\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"attr\\\",\\n      \\\"hidden\\\",\\n      false\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"input\\\",\\n      \\\"\\\",\\n      false\\n    ]\\n  ],\\n  \\\"hidden\\\": false,\\n  \\\"q\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n}\"}],\"details\":{\"xdev\":{\"tool\":\"browser\",\"mode\":\"execute\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"run\",\"code\":\"await tab.evaluate(() => { window.__ev=[]; const r=document.getElementById('global-search-results'); const i=document.getElementById('global-search-input'); new MutationObserver(m=>m.forEach(x=>window.__ev.push(['attr', x.attributeName, r.hidden]))).observe(r,{attributes:true, attributeFilter:['hidden']}); i.addEventListener('input', ()=>window.__ev.push(['input', i.value, r.hidden])); i.value='疗效'; i.dispatchEvent(new Event('input',{bubbles:true})); i.focus(); }); await tab.press('Escape'); await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r,300)); return await tab.evaluate(() => ({ev: window.__ev, hidden: document.getElementById('global-search-results').hidden, q: document.getElementById('global-search-input').value}));\"},\"tier\":\"exec\",\"inner\":{\"action\":\"run\",\"name\":\"main\",\"browser\":\"headless\",\"url\":\"http://127.0.0.1:8931/overview.html\",\"result\":\"{\\n  \\\"ev\\\": [\\n    [\\n      \\\"input\\\",\\n      \\\"疗效\\\",\\n      false\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"attr\\\",\\n      \\\"hidden\\\",\\n      true\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"attr\\\",\\n      \\\"hidden\\\",\\n      false\\n    ],\\n    [\\n      \\\"input\\\",\\n      \\\"\\\",\\n      false\\n    ]\\n  ],\\n  \\\"hidden\\\": false,\\n  \\\"q\\\": \\\"\\\"\\n}\"}}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1788079683370},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Decisive: portal handler DID run (attr hidden→true), THEN hidden→false and input cleared. So order: keydown handler hid results + preventDefault... but query still cleared and results reopened. That means preventDefault did NOT block native clearing in this Chromium (or the clear isn't the default action of this keydown), and the 'input' event from clearing reopened results via showResults(''). Net user-visible behavior in this Chromium: Escape clears the query and leaves the full default result list visible; second Escape hides panel. The code comment explicitly says preventDefault \\\"stops Chromium input[type=search] from clearing the query\\\" — but empirically in this Chromium (headless, via puppeteer CDP) it did NOT. Whether real-user Chromium behaves the same is uncertain; playwright evidence claims pass. Hmm — but the mutation trace is from MY browser session, real trusted key. So claim \\\"Escape关闭结果并保留查询\\\" is not robust: it depends on preventDefault blocking native clear, which failed here.\\n\\nActually wait — is it possible keydown handler ran but preventDefault works only if event is cancelable keydown... CDP rawKeyDown events: for input[type=search], the clearing in Chromium happens in `SearchFieldCancelButtonElement`?/ Actually Escape clearing happens in `TextFieldInputType::handleKeydownEvent`? In WebKit/Blink, Escape clearing of search field is in `SearchInputType::handleKeydownEvent` — handled BEFORE default event processing? Blink: HTMLInputElement::defaultEventHandler → textfield handles Escape. If JS preventDefault sets defaultPrevented, defaultEventHandler is skipped. Puppeteer sends RawKeyDown for Escape; maybe the renderer treats it and preventDefault from JS still applies... Empirically it did NOT apply. My session: Chrome headless (which version?). Whatever — real trusted key, observed behavior stands for this environment.\\n\\nGiven playwright evidence claims pass and my puppeteer test fails, this is a cross-harness discrepancy. As a reviewer I flag: behavior fragile — relies on preventDefault suppressing native search-clear; observed failure in headless Chromium via CDP; net effect for users could be query cleared + panel stays open showing default list. Recommend: in Escape handler ALSO set a flag to ignore the subsequent input event, or don't reopen results on empty query unless focused... Remediation concrete.\\n\\nMenu focus defect: confirmed in code (no focus call) — solid.\\n\\n768 table clipping: confirmed solid (overflow-x auto, no hint, text visually cut at edge in screenshots).\\n\\nI've spent enough. Check quickly: does the 1024 screenshot truncation exist? At 1024 stacked layout fine. At 1440 fine (overview-1440 tables looked complete).\\n\\nAlso confirm \\\"APPOIN T–PNH\\\" wrap — seen in screenshots; minor typography.\\n\\nCharts: bar charts fine; bubble chart single point with explanation note; OK. Colors: orange/blue consistent, colorblind-safe-ish; severity heatmap color scale visible. Text: Chinese natural; \\\"未列示/未公开/不适用\\\" distinguished; \\\"已报告值\\\" status present.\\n\\nNow stop server & close browser, write report.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_8N3e78KbiYImmdVdmUJM5RuE\",\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":{\"content\":\"{\\\"action\\\": \\\"close\\\", \\\"all\\\": true}\",\"i\":\"Closing browser\",\"path\":\"xd://browser\"},\"intent\":\"Closing browser\"},{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"tool_u9r4YMLXOa2iJjisY3VXp1JI\",\"name\":\"hub\",\"arguments\":{\"i\":\"Stopping report server\",\"name\":\"pnh-report\",\"op\":\"stop\"},\"intent\":\"Stopping report server\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":792,\"output\":806,\"cacheRead\":73472,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":75070,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1788079683400,\"responseId\":\"msg_GrEEmqKVrgOKWqlchCxq9R9Y\",\"duration\":19184.573250000016,\"ttft\":2907.8729169999715},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_8N3e78KbiYImmdVdmUJM5RuE\",\"toolName\":\"write\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Released 1 managed tab\"}],\"details\":{\"xdev\":{\"tool\":\"browser\",\"mode\":\"execute\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"close\",\"all\":true},\"tier\":\"exec\",\"inner\":{\"action\":\"close\",\"name\":\"main\",\"result\":\"Released 1 managed tab\"}}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1788079702624},{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"tool_u9r4YMLXOa2iJjisY3VXp1JI\",\"toolName\":\"hub\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stopped pnh-report: exited exit=1 uptime=9m33s restarts=0\"}],\"details\":{\"op\":\"stop\",\"daemon\":{\"name\":\"pnh-report\",\"id\":\"84a954b1-353f-45d4-861f-94eaef1750f6\",\"state\":\"exited\",\"createdAt\":1788079128653,\"startedAt\":1788079128654,\"readyAt\":1788079128774,\"exitedAt\":1788079702640,\"exitCode\":1,\"restartCount\":0,\"outputBytes\":974,\"owner\":\"01a051cb-a5ba-7000-b6f4-e43409c2ba0c\",\"readyMatch\":\"Serving HTTP\",\"persist\":false,\"detached\":false}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1788079702680},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Write the final report per schema. Seven domains: 文字、版式与间距、配色、图表、表格、交互、中文原生表达. Verdicts:\\n\\n- 文字： 接受（minor: \\\"APPOIN T–PNH\\\" mid-word wrap at 768 — put under 文字 or 版式； I'll make it a minor defect, not blocker... actually wrapping breaks a proper noun mid-word — for a medical manager \\\"APPOIN T–PNH\\\" is confusing. Minor, not blocking).\\n- 版式与间距： 接受（768/1024/1440 doc-level no overflow).\\n- 配色： 接受.\\n- 图表： 接受（heatmap fully visible all widths; bubble single-point justified with note).\\n- 表格： 阻断 @768 — last columns clipped, requires horizontal drag, no affordance; both engines.\\n- 交互： 阻断 — two items: (1) menu→search no auto-focus (code-confirmed; contradicts render-evidence claim); (2) Escape on search relies on preventDefault vs native clear; my Chromium repro shows query cleared + panel stays open (two Escapes needed); render evidence claims opposite. Evidence-cell Enter/Space open + Escape close + focus return verified pass (synthetic; Enter real).\\n- 中文原生表达： 接受.\\n\\nBlockers: 表格 (768) and 交互. So overall: blocked.\",\"thinkingSignature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"# Conference Participant Output: ci-phase6-final-visual-review - visual_single_object\\n\\n## Boundary Check\\n\\n- 全程只读：未修改候选报告、源代码或任何受管文件；仅启动本地静态服务器（`python3 -m http.server 8931`，指向候选目录 `reports/B/v-fixture-b-pnh-001/html`，用后已停止）和无头浏览器做真实交互复现。\\n- 未写 `runs/conference/...` 报告路径；本输出由 runner 持久化。\\n- 未做最终签收；以下为独立审阅意见，供 Codex 裁决。\\n- 摘要核验：`browser-metrics.json` 记录候选摘要 `f094848b41cf…94060e`，与会议上下文一致；我实测的即该目录内容。\\n- 未参考其他参与者输出。\\n\\n## Independent Work Product\\n\\n**总体结论：阻断（blocked）**。七域中五域接受，**表格**与**交互**两域存在可复现缺陷，且其中两处与 render-evidence 的通过声明直接矛盾。\\n\\n### 七域逐项结论\\n\\n| 域 | 结论 | 关键证据 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 文字 | 接受（1 处轻微缺陷） | 768 下试验名断词为 \\\"APPOIN\\\\nT–PNH\\\"（overview-768.png y≈5600 区段），专有名词中间断行，非技术读者会误读 |\\n| 版式与间距 | 接受 | 768/1024/1440 文档级横向溢出均为 0px（我实测 `documentElement.scrollWidth-clientWidth=0`），卡片、筛选条、导航折叠整齐 |\\n| 配色 | 接受 | 治疗组橙/对照组蓝全站一致，热图色阶与图例清晰，\\\"已报告/未公开/不适用\\\" 状态色可区分 |\\n| 图表 | 接受 | 首页与安全性页安全性热图在 768/1024/1440 两引擎均完整落入视口宽度，无需横向拖动；矩阵气泡图仅 1 点但配有\\\"APPOINT–PNH：单臂研究没有试验内对照组\\\"说明，属真实数据形态而非渲染缺失 |\\n| 表格 | **阻断 @768** | 见缺陷 T-1 |\\n| 交互 | **阻断** | 见缺陷 I-1、I-2；通过项见下 |\\n| 中文原生表达 | 接受 | \\\"点击数值查看数据依据\\\"\\\"未列示/未公开/不适用\\\"\\\"披露状态：已报告值\\\"等措辞自然、面向医学读者；未发现机翻腔或工程术语外泄 |\\n\\n### 缺陷 T-1（表格，阻断）：768 视口所有数据表末列被裁切且无任何提示\\n\\n- **页面**：安全性、首页、基线与人群总览、试验完成情况（即全部含数据表的页面）；疗效页 8 列表恰好放下，未裁切。\\n- **视口/引擎**：768 × Chromium 与 WebKit 均复现（截图 `safety-768.png`、`overview-768.png`、`baseline-overview-768.png`、`disposition-overview-768.png` 右缘可见 \\\"未列示\\\" 被裁为 \\\"未列＋半个字符\\\"）。\\n- **实测复现**：本地服务候选报告，768 视口下 `safety.html` 表格实际宽 924px、容器仅 632px（`table.scrollWidth=924 / wrap.clientWidth=632, overflow-x:auto`）；首页表格 900–1008px vs 632px。`.kz-b-table-scroll` 无滚动阴影、无\\\"可横滑\\\"提示；macOS 覆盖式滚动条不可见，医学经理不会发现右侧还有 分子/分母/状态 列。\\n- **证据矛盾**：render-evidence 对这些目标记录 `clipped_text_count=0`——该指标只测文档级溢出（确实为 0），测不到容器内表格裁切，属指标盲区，非页面无问题。\\n- **修复建议**：将 1024 已实现的堆叠卡片布局（`display:block` 逐字段行）下放到 ≤899px（现行 `@media (min-width:900px) and (max-width:1024px)` 区间在 768 反而落回宽网格，断点倒挂）；或至少加滚动提示条 + 末列 sticky。\\n\\n### 缺陷 I-1（交互，阻断项之一）：菜单展开后搜索框不自动聚焦，与证据声明相反\\n\\n- **复现**：768 下点击\\\"菜单\\\"→搜索框可见，但 `document.activeElement` 停留在 `button.site-header__menu-toggle`（真实点击与合成点击、等待 1.5s 后均如此）。\\n- **代码确认**：`assets/portal.js:263-276` 的 menu-toggle 处理器只切换 `is-open` class，**全文无任何对搜索框的 `.focus()` 调用**。\\n- **证据矛盾**：render-evidence 每条记录均声称\\\"点击'菜单'后搜索框可见=True、获得焦点=True\\\"，与实际代码行为不符。后果：不使用鼠标的用户按菜单后需再 Tab/点击一次才能输入，证据链却声称已聚焦。\\n- **修复建议**：菜单打开且 `is-open=true` 时 `searchInput.focus()`；并修正证据采集脚本断言。\\n\\n### 缺陷 I-2（交互，阻断项之二）：Escape 关闭搜索的行为脆弱，实测与声明相反\\n\\n- **声明**：render-evidence 称\\\"Escape关闭结果=True 且 保留查询=疗效\\\"。\\n- **实测**（无头 Chromium，真实按键 + MutationObserver 追踪）：输入\\\"疗效\\\"后按 Escape → 处理器确实将 `hidden` 置 true，但紧接着原生清除仍清空查询词并触发 `input` 事件，结果面板以 46 条默认列表**重新展开**；需第二次 Escape 才真正收起。即用户可见行为为\\\"清空查询 + 面板不关\\\"，与声明恰好相反。\\n- **代码根因**：`portal.js:171-176` 依赖 `event.preventDefault()` 阻止 `input[type=search]` 的原生 Escape 清空（注释亦如此写），但在我实测的 Chromium 中该阻止未生效（合成 `KeyboardEvent` 路径下处理器逻辑正常，仅真实按键复现失败）。原 playwright 证据声明通过，故存在**跨采集器不一致**，需 Codex 用 playwright 复核裁定。\\n- **修复建议**：不要依赖 preventDefault 对抗原生清空；在 Escape 处理器中同时清空后抑制紧随的 input 重开（如设 `suppressNextInput=true` 标志），或对空查询不展开默认列表。\\n\\n### 交互通过项（已实测）\\n\\n- 证据单元格（`td[tabindex=0][role=button]`）Enter 打开数据依据抽屉、Escape 关闭、关闭后焦点返回原单元格：通过（真实 Enter + 合成事件均验证；`charts.js:1103` 同时支持 Space，合成 Space 亦通过）。\\n- 抽屉内容含 披露状态=已报告值、分子/分母、来源版本，足以区分\\\"未公开/未列示\\\"与数值本身。\\n- 筛选（product=iptacopan）URL 联动、减少动态效果：证据记录通过，抽查布局未证伪。\\n\\n### 数据稀疏性判断（医学经理视角）\\n\\n- 疗效页仅 1 个终点（第24周血红蛋白应答率，APPLY 82.3% vs 1.8%、APPOINT 67.3%），安全性仅 TEAE/SAE/突破性溶血等少数事件。以 PNH 医学经理标准，缺少 LDH、输血避免、FACIT-Fatigue 等关键维度，**可比性信息偏少**，但：缺失单元格统一标\\\"未列示\\\"且在抽屉中可查证披露状态，对照组 1.8% 注明\\\"模型估计比例…不用于直接复算\\\"，单臂研究有不计算疗效差的显式说明。**未把\\\"未公开\\\"伪装成\\\"抽取丢失\\\"，也无误导性空白**；稀疏是数据真实形态，不构成视觉阻断，但建议 Codex 在签收记录中注明此候选的跨产品对比深度有限。\\n\\n## Evidence And Assumptions\\n\\n**证据（实测）**\\n- 截图：40 张 PNG 我逐一或以放大裁切方式查看了 6 页 × 3 宽度 × 2 引擎中的代表性样本（overview/safety/efficacy/matrix/baseline/disposition + responsive-search）。\\n- 实测环境：本地 http.server + 无头 Chromium，768 与 1024 视口；DOM 度量、焦点、键盘事件、MutationObserver 追踪均记录在上方结论中。\\n- 代码：`assets/portal.js:11,144-178,258-276`、`charts.js:1098-1110,1118-1139`、`report-b.css:691-694,744`、`evidence-drawer.js:625-665`。\\n\\n**推断（[INFERENCE]）**\\n- I-2 中\\\"preventDefault 未生效\\\"仅在无头 Chromium + 本工具 CDP 注入下复现；真实用户浏览器是否同样失败不确定，playwright 证据与之矛盾，故列为 Codex 复核点而非绝对定论。\\n- 截图曾疑似 baseline/matrix 文件名互换，经逐文件头部裁切直接核验后**撤回**：文件名与内容一致，系我初读缩略图误判。\\n\\n**假设**\\n- 候选服务方式（file:// 或任意静态服务）不改变上述 DOM/CSS 行为。\\n\\n## Risks, Gaps, And Verification Needs\\n\\n1. **证据可信度风险（最高影响）**：render-evidence 两处通过声明（菜单搜索自动聚焦、Escape 保留查询并关闭）与代码和实测矛盾，且 `clipped_text_count` 指标存在容器级盲区。若这两项声明失实，同文件其余声明（如 WebKit 侧键盘探针）的可信度也需打折——建议 Codex 用 playwright 对 I-1/I-2 做一次性复核，并审视该证据生成脚本的断言实现，而非只修页面。\\n2. **未覆盖项**：adherence、participant-flow、screen-failure 等其余页面无截图（本包仅 6 页）；若它们复用同一表格组件，T-1 在 768 同样存在，需补验。\\n3. **轻微缺陷（不阻断）**：768 下 \\\"APPOIN T–PNH\\\" 断词；建议 `nowrap` 或允许在连字符处断行。\\n4. **不确定项**：I-2 在真实桌面 Chromium（非无头）行为未知。\\n\\n## Recommended Next Step\\n\\n1. Codex 用 playwright 复核 I-1（菜单→搜索聚焦）与 I-2（Escape 语义）两项；若确认失实，先修正 render-evidence 采集脚本断言，再修 `portal.js`（菜单打开时 `searchInput.focus()`；Escape 增加 input 重开抑制）。\\n2. 表格断点修复：将堆叠卡片布局扩展至 ≤899px（或加滚动提示），然后重捕获 768 全套截图并校验 `table.scrollWidth ≤ wrap.clientWidth` 这一新指标（替代文档级 `horizontal_overflow_px`）。\\n3. 顺带修复 \\\"APPOIN T–PNH\\\" 断词。\\n4. 修复完成前，我的七域结论维持：表格=阻断、交互=阻断，其余五域=接受；整体建议不签发本次视觉验收。\"}],\"api\":\"anthropic-messages\",\"provider\":\"kimi-code\",\"model\":\"k3-256k\",\"usage\":{\"input\":902,\"output\":2775,\"cacheRead\":74240,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":77917,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"t